 "chapter": 1,
 "characters": {
  "GM": {
   "code": "GM",
   "name": "Gajanan Maharaj",
   "identity_paragraph": "Shri Gajanan Maharaj: a young man in the prime of youth (looks about 25 to 30), strong and well built, muscular upper arms and neck, broad chest, radiant calm handsome face, eyes half-lowered with the gaze resting on the tip of his nose, short cropped dark hair, clean-shaven, warm medium-brown skin. He wears only one old, worn, torn sleeveless bandi (a short open-front vest) of faded grey-white cloth with frayed edges, and a minimal plain off-white loincloth; otherwise bare. Barefoot, no jewellery, no beads, no forehead mark. His only belongings: a dried bottle-gourd water vessel (natural tan, narrow neck) and a small hand-made unfired clay chilim (a straight conical clay pipe, matte raw grey-brown clay, never kiln-fired).",
